      "lastReply": "A young tiger named Raju lived in the forest and loved the smell of biryani from the village nearby. One day, he sneaked into a wedding kitchen and watched the cook layer rice, spices and meat in a big pot. The cook spotted him but, instead of running, taught him the secret: patience, the right heat and a pinch of saffron at the end.\n\nRaju practised every night by the river, using wild herbs and whatever he could find. His first few tries were disasters—burnt rice, too much salt, once he added mud by mistake. But he kept going, and soon the forest filled with the smell of perfect biryani.\n\nWord spread, and animals came from far away to taste his cooking. Raju opened a small dhaba under a banyan tree, and even the villagers started visiting. He never forgot the cook who believed a tiger could learn anything, as long as he didn't give up.\n\n8:02 PM",
